# book_shop:
# CSES 1158, Book Shop (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1158), in our own words:
# a shop sells books, each with a price and a number of pages, each bought at
# most once; with a budget, the most pages whose books together cost at most budget
# (zero when no book fits). The input is a Scott list of pairs (price, pages)
# of binary naturals (corpora/library/prelude/pair) and the budget, a binary
# natural. Part of the CSES port's second batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of the (total price, total
# pages) of every subset of the books is built (the empty subset has (0, 0); the
# subsets of a book followed by the others are the subsets of the others, and the
# same with the book added), and the most pages among those whose total price is
# at most budget is taken. Its reading is exponential in the number of books even under
# tabling, since the 2^n subsets are built and summed; the replacement the family
# asks for is the 0-1 knapsack, best(budget) = max(best(budget), best(budget - price) + pages)
# for each book with the budgets descending, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces
# to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since
# subset_totals consumes the finite list of books and every other recursion
# consumes a finite list or a binary numeral. So the β reduction reaches V; the
# branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read. The program calls no
# subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable
# equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "pair")
λ pair _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ _ merge_binary_plus _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than binary_maximum _
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self books
    . books (cons (pair binary_zero binary_zero) nil)
      λ book others
      . ( λ without
          . append without
            λ. map
            ( λ total
              . total
                λ price pages
                . book
                  λ book_price book_pages
                  . pair (merge_binary_plus price book_price) λ. merge_binary_plus pages book_pages
            ) without
        ) λ. self others
  )
λ subset_totals
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self budget most totals
    . totals most
      λ total others
      . self budget
        ( total
          λ price pages
          . binary_less_than budget price most λ. binary_maximum most pages
        ) others
  )
λ most_within
. (λtuple. tuple λbooks budget. most_within budget binary_zero λ. subset_totals books)
λ book_shop
. export book_shop
